The legal texts are official texts of the Republic of South Africa. Under the Copyright Act 98 of 1978, s. 12(8)(a),
"No copyright shall subsist in official texts of a legislative, administrative or legal nature".

They were taken from:

  Department of Justice and Constitutional Development, www.justice.gov.za (retrieved 28 October 2026);
  Government Communication and Information System (GCIS), www.gov.za and info.gov.za (retrieved 28 October 2026,
  older pages through the Internet Archive);
  Information Regulator, inforegulator.org.za (retrieved 28 October 2026);
  LawLibrary (lawlibrary.org.za, Laws.Africa and AfricanLII), CC BY-NC 4.0, read only through Internet Archive
  captures and used only where no government source gives a wording (listed in REPRODUCE.md).

The terms of justice.gov.za and gov.za allow their content to be copied and distributed for non-commercial
informational or reference purposes. LawLibrary content is licensed CC BY-NC 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/); attribution: LawLibrary (lawlibrary.org.za).

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; amendment notes were removed from the text and used only to credit the
amending law; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws that made each change. The wording of
the law was not changed. None of the sources endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
